---
// Facts only; every cell traces to docs/research/buyer-need.md §5 or seo-geo-aeo.md §4 (see docs/claims.md).
const rows: Array<[string, string, string, string, string, string]> = [
  ["Integrity claim", "Hash chain, Ed25519 receipts, roots anchored to Rekor + OpenTimestamps", "None on the product or pricing page", "None; retention tiers", "No customer-facing audit log; evidence bundles for your auditor", "A permission (REVOKE), not a proof"],
  ["Verify without trusting the vendor", "Yes: npx @auditkit/verify, offline", "No", "No", "No", "n/a: you are the vendor, and so is your DBA"],
  ["Pricing", "$0 / $49 / $199 per month", "$99/mo per 1M events retained + $125/mo per SIEM stream", "2–3% of spend per month", "Not published for this feature", "Your time: 6–12 weeks for a basic build"],
  ["Default retention", "30 days / 1 year / 3 years (payloads); hashes forever", "30 days by default", "3 to 90 days", "n/a", "Whatever you set, until someone drops the partition"],
  ["Erasure without breaking the record", "Crypto-shredding per event", "Not described", "Not described", "n/a", "DELETE breaks any chain you built"],
  ["Per-tenant proofs for your customers' auditors", "Merkle path + public-log receipts", "No", "No", "No", "No"],
  ["SIEM streaming", "No; JSONL export API instead", "Yes, per-connection fee", "Yes, it is a SIEM", "No", "Build it"],
];
---
<div class="card overflow-x-auto">
  <table class="w-full min-w-[900px] text-sm">
    <thead>
      <tr class="border-b border-line text-left">
        <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-faint"></th>
        <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-accent">AuditKit</th>
        <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">WorkOS Audit Logs</th>
        <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Datadog Audit Trail</th>
        <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Drata / Vanta</th>
        <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">pgaudit / DIY Postgres</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {rows.map(([k, ...cells]) => (
        <tr class="border-b border-line last:border-0 align-top">
          <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-normal text-muted">{k}</th>
          {cells.map((c, i) => <td class:list={["px-4 py-2.5", i === 0 ? "text-fg" : "text-muted"]}>{c}</td>)}
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="mt-3 text-xs text-faint">Vendor cells from their public pricing and docs pages, fetched 2026-10-05/06 (WorkOS pricing and docs, Datadog pricing list and Audit Trail docs, Velt's build estimate). Cloud ledgers and open-source options (Azure Confidential Ledger, Google Cloud Audit Logs, immudb, Retraced) are compared on the <a href="/compare/postgres" class="underline">Postgres and self-built page</a>. We will correct any cell a vendor shows to be out of date.</p>
